module gunbc.plans.convergence_coverage_program

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn convergence_coverage_program_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Goal: every admitted operation requires its complete prerequisite chain, and success is consumed only after effectful establishment. This implementation program extends v2_compiler_architecture/ensure_closure_design D14; it does not redesign them or authorize implementation. Operator 2026-10-11 placed it under debt-payoff, not duplicate factory/v2-compiler-live membership (MembershipAmbiguous). Evidence: srv1 findings review pinned acc218340ed6e24a9ad06c550a5494307d0320bb; that review did not rerun the lab. Existing RFM/rung-drop rows remain class authorities."),
    p(text: "The gap is execution-boundary operands: shell RunArgv/RunArgvStdin/RunArgvOutcome accept program spelling/argv rather than a program runtime qualified for placement/principal. Removing an ensure therefore does not remove a required operand. D14 already owns qualified operands, restricted construction and root completion; ensure fn/ensured syntax was withdrawn. ensure_decide and ensure_reconcile classify supplied reports; ConvergedEffect constructor restriction alone proves neither effect execution nor independent observation. Preserve srv3_ensure_apt, run_microvm_network_apply’s ensure_host_tool guard and converge_typed_remote_file’s actual effect/readback routes."),
    p(text: "cc-path-census first: typed denominator of production observe/decide/apply/readback/mint paths, recording route, subject, supplied versus established facts and covering leaf or named exclusion. No repair against an unenumerated path. Existing srv1-pinned wrappers over generic cores (belt/serve/dispatch/dashboard-apply/launch/preflight/selection; selection fixed #13720) belong in that census, not copied counts."),
    p(text: "A cc-compiler-floor: execute a native-route negative control for SystemdRunProperty-list supplied to session_placement_record_write’s String list (F19/F36). direct_call_generic_type_argument_inhabitance_diags already exists; do not invent a missing generic checker. Scalar-formal InhabitanceUndecidable→advisory DeclaredTypeInhabitanceUndecided is the known class product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted. Zero blocking errors does not establish every obligation; never transfer seed findings to v2 without execution."),
    p(text: "B cc-structural-carriers: bash_build_subshell accepts arbitrary Node, while bash_fold_flatten_stmt_list reads only children 0/1 and can discard or_else behavior (F37). Establish grammar shape at construction, preserve every admitted child, refuse malformed input. Caller-only from_stmts repair does not close the shared reader; no second Bash model."),
    p(text: "C cc-qualified-operands: paths do not establish writable sockets, readable secrets or checkout capability (F02/F07/F14/F16/F35/F43–44). Owner boundary requires capability, selected providers induce dependencies, compiler carries them outward, root binds policy/placement. srv3_ensure_apt’s independent subject/package can install one thing and read another; D14 owns that specimen. Existing directory-demand repairs are precedents, not systematic completion."),
    p(text: "D cc-observation-distinctions: owned active service with broken health/release endpoint must remain distinguishable from absent, foreign/conflicting or unobservable (F11/F01/F46/F52; a_deploy_that_observes_its_own_service_cannot_repair_it). Desired→no mutation; proven absence→policy-permitted create; owned repairable drift→derived repair; conflict→refusal/admitted transition; unknown→refuse dependents. Never turn arbitrary 403 into absence or incomplete census into unconditional best effort; domain assessment, not generic satisfaction Bool."),
    p(text: "E cc-lifecycle-ownership: cover failure/retirement and all member kinds, not observed=[] for belt/publication/storage/approval/tailnet artifacts. Removing desired membership must retire previously owned objects. Before promotion establish/materialize exact candidate serving closure; after actuation independently observe that candidate running. Shared activation identity/reconciliation must cover both container and record crash gaps, dispatch/cleanup populations, foreign listeners and mutation→projection dependencies. Moving a write only moves the gap. Fleet admission is first consumer of the still-unhomed shared effectful cycle; this program must not mint another home."),
    p(text: "F cc-selection-to-use: carry environment/candidate/principal/state/source identity consistently into effects. fleet_converge_named_revision_and_branch admits branch development; universal main-only is not its restoration. Security/writable scope/concurrency/grants remain distinct prerequisites with their own authorities: ensure cannot grant permission or promise volatile capacity. Cite a_dispatch_is_gated_on_main_not_its_admitted_candidate rather than copy its rule."),
    p(text: "G cc-evidence-to-consumers: exact revision/behavior evidence must constrain the next action; v1_required_lanes_withdrawn means green required CI does not establish all workspace serving/deploy/sudoers/witness/drift obligations. An unobserved claim is not evidence; supplied inputs must never remove the last real-path execution. Preserve class controls when deleting production machinery."),
    p(text: "cc-guaranteed-cleanup: use std.upsert_decision ensure, independent readback and named driver. Live owner/held→Noop; proven-ended owner/still-held→Apply; inaccessible/unknown→Refuse and retain charge, never free on doubt. First compute seats via work_provider_local.compute_recover_attempt (F75, a_held_compute_seat_has_no_in_corpus_discharge); keep failed checkpoint units F68, supervisors F72, half-spawn F20/F21 and leftover lease files rostered. Ledger: https://claude.ai/artifact/7AMGHuyVXu1U7bFXDnbG1M."),
    p(text: "Order: census; A/B in parallel; C; D/E against enumerated member/probe scope; F/G against those operations; cleanup after hold/release census. Red: consumer still typechecks after its prerequisite-producing ensure is removed. Positive: only effectful mint yields qualified operand, raw identity cannot bind. Every leaf retains its RFM discriminating red; declaration or review never replaces execution."),
  ]
}

data convergence_coverage_program_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "convergence-coverage-program",
  title: "Convergence coverage: the ensure chain to the execution boundary",
  body: convergence_coverage_program_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this document when every production path in the census either consumes a qualified operand minted on the D14 effectful route or carries a named exclusion with a DESIGN section 3b reason, each covering leaf's handback is met, and the roadmap project convergence-coverage is accepted. At that point the carriers, witnesses and rung-drop rows are the authority, and this program document would be a second statement of them.") }
}
